UPDATE goals SET description = 'The travellers halt for the evening at the Forsaken Inn, a dreary and dilapidated establishment standing as a lonely marker just east of the Bree-land. Choosing to avoid the gloom of the main building, the company establishes their camp within the relative shelter of the stables. Although the setting is bleak, spirits remain high with the knowledge that the friendly lights of the Prancing Pony are merely a day''s march to the west. This rough accommodation serves as the final boundary between the long, perilous road behind them and the welcoming civilisation just ahead.' WHERE distance = 3423 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Bree: arrive at The Prancing Pony (Distance: 3439)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The company rides back into Bree and halts at The Prancing Pony, where Barliman Butterbur stares at them as if seeing ghosts. The worthy landlord had long since given the hobbits up for dead, and he frankly admits his astonishment at seeing them return as lordly figures, far changed from the frightened runaways he once sheltered. As they sit by the fire once more, the travellers listen to Butterbur''s anxious tales of trouble in the North and ruffians gathering on the borders. It becomes clear that while the great darkness has fallen in the South, smaller evils still linger to threaten the peace of the Shire.' WHERE distance = 3439 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: The Old Forest begins to the south (Distance: 3455)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The travellers rode westward along the East Road, leaving the comfort of Bree behind. To their left, the land fell away into the dark, tangled canopy of the Old Forest, visible once more against the horizon. It was here that Gandalf chose to part ways with the company, turning his horse south to visit Tom Bombadil in his mossy house. Frodo and his companions continued alone towards the Brandywine Bridge, no longer daunted by the ancient trees that had once seemed so threatening.' WHERE distance = 3455 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach the Brandywine Bridge (Distance: 3479)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The four travellers rode down the Causeway to the Brandywine Bridge, only to find their way blocked by a great gate spiked with iron. Where the bridge had once stood open to all, now new guardhouses loomed in the twilight, and nervous Shirrifs emerged to enforce the Chief''s harsh rules. Frodo and his companions, their mail clanking softly beneath their cloaks, gazed upon these grim changes with a heavy realisation. The dark shadow they had fought in the East had cast a long gloom even over the borders of the Shire.' WHERE distance = 3479 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Frogmorton (Distance: 3501)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The four travellers arrived at the water-surrounded village of Frogmorton, only to find the road barred by a large troop of Shirriffs armed with staves. Instead of a warm welcome at The Floating Log, the companions were officiously halted and declared under arrest by order of the Chief at Bag End. Merry and Pippin treated the situation with amused contempt, their mail-clad stature towering over the flustered hobbit-guards who tried to enforce the new Rules. It was a stark sign of the troubles that had taken root in the Shire, turning a once-friendly hamlet into a place of suspicion and closed doors.' WHERE distance = 3501 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach Bag End (Distance: 3524)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'Frodo and his companions ascend the Hill to stand once more before the round green door of Bag End, finding the comfortable smial sadly altered by its occupation as Sharkey''s headquarters. Upon the very doorstep where the quest began, the hobbits witness the end of Saruman and Grima Wormtongue, watching as the wizard''s spirit dissolves like grey mist in a wind from the West. The scouring is complete, and though the Shire has been marred, the travellers can finally set down their packs in the place they once left so long ago. With the shadow finally lifted, Samwise turns his thoughts to the gift of Galadriel and the healing of the wounded land.' WHERE distance = 3524 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach Stock Road (Distance: 3538)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'Frodo and Sam rode quietly from Hobbiton, guiding their ponies down to the Stock Road to begin the journey that would lead them to the sea. The travellers passed through the familiar landscapes of the Eastfarthing, retracing the path of their initial flight, though now the air was free of the fear of Black Riders. This road guided them towards the Woody End, where the Last Riding of the Keepers awaited their arrival in the twilight. It was a solemn departure, carrying the Ring-bearer away from the home he had saved but could no longer truly inhabit.' WHERE distance = 3538 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach the point where the road splits (Distance: 3561)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The hobbits halted their ponies at the junction where the lane from the Woody End met the Great East Road. It was here that the Last Riding of the Keepers emerged from the twilight, with Elrond and Galadriel bearing the Three Rings of Power openly on their fingers. Riding beside the Elven-lords was an elderly Bilbo Baggins, who woke from a nap to cheerfully announce his readiness for this final adventure. The reunited company turned their faces westward, travelling in silence through the cooling air as they began the long road to the Sea.' WHERE distance = 3561 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Camp in the open lands (Distance: 3614)
